   "evidence": "In the diff, `hpiece` repeats `rw [\u2190 Isometry.map_euclideanHausdorffMeasure_restrict ..., (measurableEmbedding_addRight _).ae_map_iff, ae_restrict_halfDiscFlatSegment_iff] at h` after calling `(W1p.translate_mem_halfDiscFlatTraceZeroSubmodule_iff ...).1`. A grep of the diff shows no lemma relating the image of `halfDiscFlatSegment` under translation to `Icc (c - \u03c1) (c + \u03c1)`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Sobolev/LipschitzDomain/HalfDisc/FlatTrace.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public `image_add_halfDiscFlatSegment : (\u00b7 + toLp 2 (0, c)) '' halfDiscFlatSegment \u03c1 = (fun t => toLp 2 (0, t)) '' Icc (c - \u03c1) (c + \u03c1)` in `HalfDisc/Basic.lean`. Alternatively, add an interval-form corollary of the iff (`\u2200\u1d50 t \u2202volume.restrict (Icc (c - \u03c1) (c + \u03c1)), trace (toLp 2 (0, t)) = 0`) and use it in `hpiece`.",
   "issue": "`W1p.translate_mem_halfDiscFlatTraceZeroSubmodule_iff` states its condition over `(\u00b7 + toLp 2 (0, c)) '' halfDiscFlatSegment \u03c1`, while its docstring and the module doc promise the subsegment `[c - \u03c1, c + \u03c1]`. No lemma identifies the two. As a result, `hpiece` in `mem_halfDiscFlatTraceZeroSubmodule_of_forall_translate` reverses the iff's own rewrites: it re-applies `\u2190 Isometry.map_euclideanHausdorffMeasure_restrict`, `ae_map_iff`, the private `ae_restrict_halfDiscFlatSegment_iff`, `restrict_image_emb` and `image_add_const_Icc` to recover the interval form.",
   "line": 0
  }
 ],
